    {
      "id": "t1437",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 1478,
      "width": 594.0,
      "height": 75.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0437",
      "seed": 20059,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 38681,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "Build \u00b7 Belongs to the consuming project \u00b7 `gate.py --root <path>`, defaulting to\n`kit.ROOT`; the library already takes `root` everywhere, so only the CLI entry point pins\nit \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 medium \u2014 the parameterisation is proven by the selftest passing temp\ntrees, but the SCRIPT-location half is undesigned: `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` expands nowhere\nin this repo and `$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` measured unset \u00b7 \u2014",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Build \u00b7 Belongs to the consuming project \u00b7 `gate.py --root <path>`, defaulting to\n`kit.ROOT`; the library already takes `root` everywhere, so only the CLI entry point pins\nit \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 medium \u2014 the parameterisation is proven by the selftest passing temp\ntrees, but the SCRIPT-location half is undesigned: `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` expands nowhere\nin this repo and `$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` measured unset \u00b7 \u2014",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1438",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 1565,
      "width": 587.4000000000001,
      "height": 60.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0438",
      "seed": 20066,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 38694,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "Build \u00b7 The twenty-category taxonomy \u00b7 move the twenty codes out of `kit.py` into the\nproject's own `categories.md`, so a consuming project extends rather than inherits a\nhardcode \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 high \u2014 the disposition file already has to exist and already lists\nall twenty \u00b7 \u2014",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Build \u00b7 The twenty-category taxonomy \u00b7 move the twenty codes out of `kit.py` into the\nproject's own `categories.md`, so a consuming project extends rather than inherits a\nhardcode \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 high \u2014 the disposition file already has to exist and already lists\nall twenty \u00b7 \u2014",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1439",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 1637,
      "width": 594.0,
      "height": 60.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0439",
      "seed": 20073,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 38707,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "Build \u00b7 Refusal from outside the model \u00b7 ship the checker in `tools/` and give it an entry\npoint a consuming project's own CI can invoke \u00b7 temporary \u00b7 low \u2014 Kerd's CI audits Kerd; a\nconsuming project gets the skills' judgment, not the machine's refusal, and every external\noption scores \u25cb here \u00b7 the first consuming project that runs the audit against itself",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Build \u00b7 Refusal from outside the model \u00b7 ship the checker in `tools/` and give it an entry\npoint a consuming project's own CI can invoke \u00b7 temporary \u00b7 low \u2014 Kerd's CI audits Kerd; a\nconsuming project gets the skills' judgment, not the machine's refusal, and every external\noption scores \u25cb here \u00b7 the first consuming project that runs the audit against itself",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1440",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 1709,
      "width": 594.0,
      "height": 45.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0440",
      "seed": 20080,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 38720,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "StrictDoc \u00b7 Machine-readable by stdlib \u00b7 write a stdlib parser for `.sdoc` rather than\nusing the JSON export, which requires the tool to run \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 medium \u2014 the format is\nregular enough to parse, but this is work the adoption was meant to avoid \u00b7 \u2014",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "StrictDoc \u00b7 Machine-readable by stdlib \u00b7 write a stdlib parser for `.sdoc` rather than\nusing the JSON export, which requires the tool to run \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 medium \u2014 the format is\nregular enough to parse, but this is work the adoption was meant to avoid \u00b7 \u2014",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1441",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 1766,
      "width": 594.0,
      "height": 105.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0441",
      "seed": 20087,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 38733,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "StrictDoc \u00b7 The five-state lifecycle \u00b7 declare a custom grammar field `TYPE:\nSingleChoice(proposed, qualified, final, superseded, dropped)` with `REQUIRED: True`,\nwhich refuses a bad value by name and an omission by name \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 high \u2014 built and\nverified hands-on against a Kerd-shaped grammar; but it IS a countermeasure, because the\nshipped `STATUS` field is an unconstrained free string (`STATUS: BANANA_NOT_A_REAL_STATUS`\nround-tripped clean, and the `Draft / Active / Deleted` rule in the grammar is dead code\nreferenced by no production) \u00b7 \u2014",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "StrictDoc \u00b7 The five-state lifecycle \u00b7 declare a custom grammar field `TYPE:\nSingleChoice(proposed, qualified, final, superseded, dropped)` with `REQUIRED: True`,\nwhich refuses a bad value by name and an omission by name \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 high \u2014 built and\nverified hands-on against a Kerd-shaped grammar; but it IS a countermeasure, because the\nshipped `STATUS` field is an unconstrained free string (`STATUS: BANANA_NOT_A_REAL_STATUS`\nround-tripped clean, and the `Draft / Active / Deleted` rule in the grammar is dead code\nreferenced by no production) \u00b7 \u2014",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1442",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 1883,
      "width": 594.0,
      "height": 45.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0442",
      "seed": 20094,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 38746,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "Doorstop \u00b7 The same files \u00b7 accept the `reqs/**/` tree as the register's declared home; it\ncannot annotate `docs/product/<slug>.md` at all \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 low \u2014 a parallel layout by\ndesign, and the tool's whole merge story depends on it \u00b7 \u2014",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Doorstop \u00b7 The same files \u00b7 accept the `reqs/**/` tree as the register's declared home; it\ncannot annotate `docs/product/<slug>.md` at all \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 low \u2014 a parallel layout by\ndesign, and the tool's whole merge story depends on it \u00b7 \u2014",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1443",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 1940,
      "width": 580.8000000000001,
      "height": 45.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0443",
      "seed": 20101,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 38759,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "Doorstop \u00b7 No artifact scatter \u00b7 flatten to one document per category rather than per\nitem, trading merge-friendliness for file count \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 low \u2014 file-per-item is HOW\nit earns clean diffs; the evidence states the scatter cannot be configured away \u00b7 \u2014",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Doorstop \u00b7 No artifact scatter \u00b7 flatten to one document per category rather than per\nitem, trading merge-friendliness for file count \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 low \u2014 file-per-item is HOW\nit earns clean diffs; the evidence states the scatter cannot be configured away \u00b7 \u2014",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1444",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 1997,
      "width": 594.0,
      "height": 45.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0444",
      "seed": 20108,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 38772,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "Doorstop \u00b7 Claude Code friendly \u00b7 give the model the filename convention and the per-\ndocument `.doorstop.yml` so capture is a Write to a computable path \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 medium \u2014\nthe UID IS the filename, so the model must compute the next free number before writing \u00b7 \u2014",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Doorstop \u00b7 Claude Code friendly \u00b7 give the model the filename convention and the per-\ndocument `.doorstop.yml` so capture is a Write to a computable path \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 medium \u2014\nthe UID IS the filename, so the model must compute the next free number before writing \u00b7 \u2014",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1445",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 2054,
      "width": 587.4000000000001,
      "height": 45.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0445",
      "seed": 20115,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 38785,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "Doorstop \u00b7 The producer's ID format \u00b7 pass `-s -` at every document creation; the default\nseparator is empty and yields `UX001` \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 high \u2014 verified hands-on, `FUN-001`\nand `UX-001` both produced verbatim \u00b7 \u2014",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Doorstop \u00b7 The producer's ID format \u00b7 pass `-s -` at every document creation; the default\nseparator is empty and yields `UX001` \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 high \u2014 verified hands-on, `FUN-001`\nand `UX-001` both produced verbatim \u00b7 \u2014",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1446",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 2111,
      "width": 594.0,
      "height": 60.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0446",
      "seed": 20122,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 38798,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "Doorstop \u00b7 The twenty-category taxonomy \u00b7 model the categories as documents under one\nsynthetic root, since a second root is rejected, and validate the set with our own checker\n\u00b7 permanent \u00b7 low \u2014 the tree is single-rooted by design and a flat taxonomy is not\nexpressible natively \u00b7 \u2014",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Doorstop \u00b7 The twenty-category taxonomy \u00b7 model the categories as documents under one\nsynthetic root, since a second root is rejected, and validate the set with our own checker\n\u00b7 permanent \u00b7 low \u2014 the tree is single-rooted by design and a flat taxonomy is not\nexpressible natively \u00b7 \u2014",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1447",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 2183,
      "width": 594.0,
      "height": 60.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
